    <item>
      <title>OSI Network Model</title>
      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/osi-network-model/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/osi-network-model/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h4 id=&#34;disclaimer-image-is-generated-using-chatgpt&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DISCLAIMER:&lt;/strong&gt; Image is generated using &lt;code&gt;ChatGPT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To understand how networking works from the ground up, imagine the &lt;strong&gt;OSI Model&lt;/strong&gt;, the standard 7-layer framework for networking as a postal service delivering an international gift package.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When sending a letter or package, you don&amp;rsquo;t just throw an item into the air and hope it arrives.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You write a message, translate or wrap it if needed, put it in an envelope, write addresses, hand it to a driver, and ship it over roads or cables.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
